7: /**
8:  * Covers the routing-shape check (12b-routing-shape) in parent-skill-check.cjs:
9:  * a canon-shaped hub and packet pass at exit 0, and each rule fails on its own
10:  * fixture — short routing prose past its budget (RS-001), a machine-router
11:  * section or a stray router block left in SKILL.md (RS-002), a section that is
12:  * not last (RS-003), a sibling ROUTER.md that is missing, not a regular file or
13:  * outside the skill folder (RS-004) and a body carrying no working pointer to
14:  * it (RS-005). The pointer is one line holding a link whose target is exactly
15:  * `ROUTER.md` once a leading `./` and any #anchor are stripped, so a heading
16:  * line counts, while an angle-bracket target, trailing text, a label split
17:  * across lines, a link that lives only in the frontmatter and a nested target
18:  * do not. The known-debt ledger tolerates a recorded shape while still failing
19:  * one that grew past a recorded limit, one that raised a code its entry never
20:  * recorded, a machine block left in the routing prose and a ROUTER.md that is
21:  * not a missing regular file, and a packet with no router file is tolerated by
22:  * check 12a only when its entry records RS-004. The checker
23:  * resolves its contract libraries from the repository root, so the temp
24:  * fixtures are audited against the same code as a live hub, and the ledger and
25:  * skills-root overrides keep the live ledger out of every case.
26:  */
